# Comments

Comment **why**, not **what**. No decorative banners.

## File header

At most one line when purpose is not obvious from the path:

```py
"""Resolve CI necessity for local vs publish purposes."""
```

Skip headers on tiny helpers whose name is the contract.

## Sections

Blank line + short lowercase label. No `# ---` or `====` banners:

```py
# admission

def admit(...):
    ...
```

## Inline

Never trailing `# comment` on code lines. Put the comment on the line above.

## When to comment

- Sync points (impact registry <-> runners, request DTOs <-> CLI)
- Platform quirks and intentional non-obvious choices
- Privacy / mutation safety gotchas

Do not restate identifiers or add category labels (`# helpers`, `# utils`).

## Format

- ASCII `-` in comments that mirror user-facing harness strings
- Agent prose in `.cursor/` may use em dash for readability
- Max ~100 columns; wrap on phrase boundaries
- Same indent as the block below; no column-pretty alignment games
